(4052720, 576542, 83080, '<td valign="top">This is my first serious entry on DPC (my previous ''sacred'' entry was intended as a joke) and I''m a little surprised it didn''t even make it out of _4_ territory.  I really thought more people would be able to see it, as posthumous commented, with a unique sense of "false perspective".  I am a string player and have taken (and seen) countless ordinary pictures of the beautiful lines on these instruments as strangeghost suggests, but I intended to catch something a little deeper in the finish of the instrument against that well defined f-hole.<br/> <br/>To score well I supose subtle artistic intent may unfortunately be lost in the voting.  I came here to learn the basics of composing and executing shots and, like any art, it''s usually best to master the basics and "standard repertoire" before going out on a limb.  Still, I like this shot.<br/> <br/>-----<br/> <br/>Yup, just revisited this after several months and several entries that scored higher.  I still like this a great deal and think it was badly under rated, although I understand now why it did not do well in this voting environment.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-04-08 22:15:59.</i></td>', 'This is my first serious entry on DPC (my previous ''sacred'' entry was intended as a joke) and I''m a little surprised it didn''t even make it out of _4_ territory.  I really thought more people would be able to see it, as posthumous commented, with a unique sense of "false perspective".  I am a string player and have taken (and seen) countless ordinary pictures of the beautiful lines on these instruments as strangeghost suggests, but I intended to catch something a little deeper in the finish of the instrument against that well defined f-hole. To score well I supose subtle artistic intent may unfortunately be lost in the voting.  I came here to learn the basics of composing and executing shots and, like any art, it''s usually best to master the basics and "standard repertoire" before going out on a limb.  Still, I like this shot. ----- Yup, just revisited this after several months and several entries that scored higher.  I still like this a great deal and think it was badly under rated, although I understand now why it did not do well in this voting environment.', '2007-09-03 09:59:11.000000', '2008-04-08 23:15:59.000000', 0),
