(4065195, 577708, 74829, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by smardaz:</b></div><hr/><i> whats the story here? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>thanks for your interest, smardaz~<br/> <br/>some fisherman (Chinese) always sun dry the seafood,if they caught too much or the fish they caught were not valuable enough to make their living, so they will rather sun dry the seafood and keep it for themselves<br/> <br/>in this photo the fisherman is sun drying the fishes, probably the fish will used for making porridge.. the sun drying will process about three days under the sun.. and the fishes can be kept for a long time afterwards<br/> <br/>its a way of the fisherman living</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz: whats the story here?   thanks for your interest, smardaz~ some fisherman (Chinese) always sun dry the seafood,if they caught too much or the fish they caught were not valuable enough to make their living, so they will rather sun dry the seafood and keep it for themselves in this photo the fisherman is sun drying the fishes, probably the fish will used for making porridge.. the sun drying will process about three days under the sun.. and the fishes can be kept for a long time afterwards its a way of the fisherman living', '2007-09-06 12:17:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4065229, 575582, 74829, '<td valign="top">Originally posted by smardaz:<br/>whats the story here?<br/> <br/>thanks for your interest on my photo<a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=577708" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">"Wanna Swim"</a>, smardaz~<br/> <br/>some fisherman (Chinese) always sun dry the seafood,if they caught too much or the fish they caught were not valuable enough to make their living, so they will rather sun dry the seafood and keep it for themselves<br/> <br/>in this photo the fisherman is sun drying the fishes, probably the fish will used for making porridge.. the sun drying will process about three days under the sun.. and the fishes can be kept for a long time afterwards<br/> <br/>its a way of the fisherman living<br/> <br/>by the way, i love your photo "wisdom of the cat" the lighting from the side is just lovely<br/> <br/>ryan</td>', 'Originally posted by smardaz:whats the story here? thanks for your interest on my photo"Wanna Swim", smardaz~ some fisherman (Chinese) always sun dry the seafood,if they caught too much or the fish they caught were not valuable enough to make their living, so they will rather sun dry the seafood and keep it for themselves in this photo the fisherman is sun drying the fishes, probably the fish will used for making porridge.. the sun drying will process about three days under the sun.. and the fishes can be kept for a long time afterwards its a way of the fisherman living by the way, i love your photo "wisdom of the cat" the lighting from the side is just lovely ryan', '2007-09-06 12:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
