(4071986, 577590, 47483, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Siggav:</b></div><hr/><i> zxaar - you''re right, and we were very close this time around. It''s actually worse coming in 6th though (I did that in the without a net challenge). Then you''re one off getting an honourable mention on your profile. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>hi, I hope you have not minded what I wrote. I just did not want to write routine - wonderful picture comment. So I wrote in a different way. <br/>I was happy that I broke 6.5 mark and along with that I finished in top 10. This is enough for me.<br/> <br/>and yes, in this challenge also now you are 6th. he he he.<br/> <br/>But I felt bad for hotpasta (his image got dq), he is very nice person, I always get very encouraging comments from him. He understands photography.</td>', 'Originally posted by Siggav: zxaar - you''re right, and we were very close this time around. It''s actually worse coming in 6th though (I did that in the without a net challenge). Then you''re one off getting an honourable mention on your profile.   hi, I hope you have not minded what I wrote. I just did not want to write routine - wonderful picture comment. So I wrote in a different way. I was happy that I broke 6.5 mark and along with that I finished in top 10. This is enough for me. and yes, in this challenge also now you are 6th. he he he. But I felt bad for hotpasta (his image got dq), he is very nice person, I always get very encouraging comments from him. He understands photography.', '2007-09-08 10:10:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4072992, 575731, 69008, '<td valign="top">I feel that more depth of field by using a smaller aperture would have made a difference. The DPC voters seem to like everything being sharp.  Another improvment would have been to do something with the lower right corner, where there is something, which I assume is a shoulder strap, that distracts from the primary subject, the lips.  A piece of light or dark cloth on the shoulder and up to the side of the face would have eliminated that area, or maybe a little closer in with the camera. <br/>A little makeup (lipstick) for a dash of color and a title to draw attention to the lips, and hint of action, like "Spicy Kiss" may have helped a little too. <br/>I am not exactly sure what you did to get the image, I am guessing that it is your face in a bowl?  <br/>It is a great concept shot which just needed for the original to lead to a carefully planned reshoot. <br/>That is the worst that I can do with it. I hope that you are not offended. <br/>Don''t take all this too seriously, as I seem to not know what I am doing according to the below 5''s on my two current challenge images. : )</td>', 'I feel that more depth of field by using a smaller aperture would have made a difference. The DPC voters seem to like everything being sharp.  Another improvment would have been to do something with the lower right corner, where there is something, which I assume is a shoulder strap, that distracts from the primary subject, the lips.  A piece of light or dark cloth on the shoulder and up to the side of the face would have eliminated that area, or maybe a little closer in with the camera. A little makeup (lipstick) for a dash of color and a title to draw attention to the lips, and hint of action, like "Spicy Kiss" may have helped a little too. I am not exactly sure what you did to get the image, I am guessing that it is your face in a bowl?  It is a great concept shot which just needed for the original to lead to a carefully planned reshoot. That is the worst that I can do with it. I hope that you are not offended. Don''t take all this too seriously, as I seem to not know what I am doing according to the below 5''s on my two current challenge images. : )', '2007-09-08 18:51:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(4073145, 575731, 66952, '<td valign="top">hmmm....I gave this a 4, so I should comment. I think for me, the technical quality is fine. Focus, lighting, DOF, etc, are all good. I might have cropped off the dark stuff on the right side, but that''s personal opinion. Usually, if the technicals are all in place, I would give an image at least a 6, but I think when I saw this, I instantly went, ewww...ick, gave it a 4, and moved on to the next photo before I could really look at it closely. So there you have it for me...<br/></td>', 'hmmm....I gave this a 4, so I should comment. I think for me, the technical quality is fine. Focus, lighting, DOF, etc, are all good. I might have cropped off the dark stuff on the right side, but that''s personal opinion. Usually, if the technicals are all in place, I would give an image at least a 6, but I think when I saw this, I instantly went, ewww...ick, gave it a 4, and moved on to the next photo before I could really look at it closely. So there you have it for me...', '2007-09-08 20:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(4073527, 575731, 49804, '<td valign="top">in response to your critique request, i think the main reason for the low score was that it lacks a range of colors, there arent any colors that pop, it could also stand a little more contrast, nonetheless, a nice shot, and dont let voters offend you about your work, if you like it, then dont worry what others think</td>', 'in response to your critique request, i think the main reason for the low score was that it lacks a range of colors, there arent any colors that pop, it could also stand a little more contrast, nonetheless, a nice shot, and dont let voters offend you about your work, if you like it, then dont worry what others think', '2007-09-08 23:34:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4073531, 575731, 16197, '<td valign="top">Sorry I didn''t comment on the image earlier, I was just being a dork.  For me, I think the chin should be down more for one.  Also, when I think spicy I think chili peppers, so maybe instead of greens and browns, if the flakes where yellow, red, and orange I think it would have really set the ''spicy'' feel.  Also, the thumb doesn''t have the greatest appeal.  At first I looked at it and thought icky, but than thought maybe it was freckles. as I opened to the larger view I saw something else.<br/> <br/>Well these are my two cents for what they are worth.</td>', 'Sorry I didn''t comment on the image earlier, I was just being a dork.  For me, I think the chin should be down more for one.  Also, when I think spicy I think chili peppers, so maybe instead of greens and browns, if the flakes where yellow, red, and orange I think it would have really set the ''spicy'' feel.  Also, the thumb doesn''t have the greatest appeal.  At first I looked at it and thought icky, but than thought maybe it was freckles. as I opened to the larger view I saw something else. Well these are my two cents for what they are worth.', '2007-09-08 23:37:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074125, 577649, 43073, '<td valign="top">You''ve gotten the technical critiques you need, so I''ll just say I want to float across the landscape you''ve shown us, gently and slowly on a soft summer breeze.</td>', 'You''ve gotten the technical critiques you need, so I''ll just say I want to float across the landscape you''ve shown us, gently and slowly on a soft summer breeze.', '2007-09-09 03:43:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074129, 577664, 43073, '<td valign="top">Wonderful complementary shades here; well conceived and executed, especially at the picture taking stage (I never would have thought of cutting flowers!). Well done.</td>', 'Wonderful complementary shades here; well conceived and executed, especially at the picture taking stage (I never would have thought of cutting flowers!). Well done.', '2007-09-09 03:44:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074867, 575861, 43073, '<td valign="top">So delightfully red. Sometimes I forget how wonderful red is. Thanks for reminding me. I like this image and its strong push to force the viewer to look at the stem (it is what kept the apple alive while it was on the tree), though, of course, viewers have their own ideas and would rather look at the soft bits.</td>', 'So delightfully red. Sometimes I forget how wonderful red is. Thanks for reminding me. I like this image and its strong push to force the viewer to look at the stem (it is what kept the apple alive while it was on the tree), though, of course, viewers have their own ideas and would rather look at the soft bits.', '2007-09-09 12:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074870, 577213, 43073, '<td valign="top">Delightfully fun image, made me smile, nicely captured and presented; making it a bit larger in the frame for this challenge was probably what the viewers were looking for (as a guess, I don''t usually "get" the voters here).</td>', 'Delightfully fun image, made me smile, nicely captured and presented; making it a bit larger in the frame for this challenge was probably what the viewers were looking for (as a guess, I don''t usually "get" the voters here).', '2007-09-09 12:58:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074873, 577519, 43073, '<td valign="top">I think we should create blue light districts throughout the world just to provide a place for people to use this bulb. Wonderful, subtle shades of blue with lighting to die for and a perfectly chosen depth of field. Delightful.</td>', 'I think we should create blue light districts throughout the world just to provide a place for people to use this bulb. Wonderful, subtle shades of blue with lighting to die for and a perfectly chosen depth of field. Delightful.', '2007-09-09 13:01:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074990, 577025, 43073, '<td valign="top">Intricate, flowing lines, shades and tones sent from heaven, delightfully shot and shown to us here. Congrats on a top 5 with this one!</td>', 'Intricate, flowing lines, shades and tones sent from heaven, delightfully shot and shown to us here. Congrats on a top 5 with this one!', '2007-09-09 14:07:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(4074998, 577086, 43073, '<td valign="top">Golden niblets that are really golden; I love that you avoided any temptation to go with a shallow depth of field here; the sharpness throughout adds wonderfully to the glowing, tasty feeling.</td>', 'Golden niblets that are really golden; I love that you avoided any temptation to go with a shallow depth of field here; the sharpness throughout adds wonderfully to the glowing, tasty feeling.', '2007-09-09 14:09:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4075014, 577482, 43073, '<td valign="top">"The sun''ll come up, to-morrow" goes the song. But sometimes I wonder if it''s true, and in the dead of night, I awake, wondering if this is the first day that it won''t. I go to the shore and I wait. And it is not until that first light, before the sun is up, when the sun''s color washes the earth more gently, more subtly than at any other time, that I can rest again, knowing, the sun <i>will</i> come up. No question this meets the challenge to my mind, and it captures a time most of us don''t make the effort to see (even if we''re awake when it happens). Lovely.</td>', '"The sun''ll come up, to-morrow" goes the song. But sometimes I wonder if it''s true, and in the dead of night, I awake, wondering if this is the first day that it won''t. I go to the shore and I wait. And it is not until that first light, before the sun is up, when the sun''s color washes the earth more gently, more subtly than at any other time, that I can rest again, knowing, the sun will come up. No question this meets the challenge to my mind, and it captures a time most of us don''t make the effort to see (even if we''re awake when it happens). Lovely.', '2007-09-09 14:18:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(4075020, 577385, 43073, '<td valign="top">Oh to walk, even in a dream, among flowers of this shade and tone, to be one with them, even just in my own mind. Wonderful choices here for subject, shooting, and processing. I''m glad you saw it and showed it to us.</td>', 'Oh to walk, even in a dream, among flowers of this shade and tone, to be one with them, even just in my own mind. Wonderful choices here for subject, shooting, and processing. I''m glad you saw it and showed it to us.', '2007-09-09 14:20:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4075024, 577506, 43073, '<td valign="top">Wonderful capture; this is probably what my eye would look like if someone was trying to do a macro of it; somehow I still feel an expression here, even without the context of the rest of the face to confirm it. Nice.</td>', 'Wonderful capture; this is probably what my eye would look like if someone was trying to do a macro of it; somehow I still feel an expression here, even without the context of the rest of the face to confirm it. Nice.', '2007-09-09 14:21:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4075049, 577437, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is a great fill the frame shot.  Love the closeup and the intensity of the stare.  The green leaves are a great complement to the kitty''s eye color.</td>', 'This is a great fill the frame shot.  Love the closeup and the intensity of the stare.  The green leaves are a great complement to the kitty''s eye color.', '2007-09-09 14:30:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4075189, 577437, 15711, '<td valign="top">Had I not known better, I''d have thought it was our kitty Rose, except she has ONE black whisker.  Nice job.</td>', 'Had I not known better, I''d have thought it was our kitty Rose, except she has ONE black whisker.  Nice job.', '2007-09-09 15:33:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4075506, 577664, 78196, '<td valign="top">Original idea very cleverly executed. I''m very surprised this didn''t score higher.</td>', 'Original idea very cleverly executed. I''m very surprised this didn''t score higher.', '2007-09-09 18:23:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4078403, 577180, 81783, '<td valign="top">Very intense.  Love the photo &amp; the details.</td>', 'Very intense.  Love the photo & the details.', '2007-09-10 15:51:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4078978, 577725, 24454, '<td valign="top">Dang Enzo!!!  Makes you kinda confused about what''s okay and what isn''t, huh?   I have been rather paranoid ever since my dq over what I swear was less editing than I did in a ribbon winning basic editing challenge where I used the same technique!!<br/> <br/>I''m sorry this got dq''d !!!!<br/> <br/></td>', 'Dang Enzo!!!  Makes you kinda confused about what''s okay and what isn''t, huh?   I have been rather paranoid ever since my dq over what I swear was less editing than I did in a ribbon winning basic editing challenge where I used the same technique!! I''m sorry this got dq''d !!!! ', '2007-09-10 19:14:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4079300, 577582, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals: The lighting is nicely dynamic.  We see a nice play among the petals.  <br/>The feel: Although the challenge is Fill the Frame, the good ones had a purpose for filling it.  What is the purpose for the tight crop here?  I''m not sure I get one.  I''ve seen cropped roses before though that did accomplish this.  Usually they had very delicate lighting, worked on an almost abstract level, or had a secondary subject like a waterdrop or a bug.<br/> <br/>The game: With 137 challenges under your belt, I''m pretty sure you knew what you were getting into when you entered a heavily filtered shot like this. ;)  Should have saved it for impressionism.<br/></td>', 'Technicals: The lighting is nicely dynamic.  We see a nice play among the petals.  The feel: Although the challenge is Fill the Frame, the good ones had a purpose for filling it.  What is the purpose for the tight crop here?  I''m not sure I get one.  I''ve seen cropped roses before though that did accomplish this.  Usually they had very delicate lighting, worked on an almost abstract level, or had a secondary subject like a waterdrop or a bug. The game: With 137 challenges under your belt, I''m pretty sure you knew what you were getting into when you entered a heavily filtered shot like this. ;)  Should have saved it for impressionism.', '2007-09-10 21:30:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4079313, 577690, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals:  I think there is a color cast here.  The middle of the flower looks "off" to me.  It is either that or actual oversaturation.  Sometimes we jack that saturation up just too far (and I''m as guilty of that as anybody).  Composition may have improved without the second sunflower in the corner.<br/> <br/>The feel:  I mentioned this on another Fill the Frame, but what is the purpose of the tight crop other than to meet the challenge?  The best pictures in this challenge conveyed something by their tight crop.<br/> <br/>The game:  OK, you''ve been around long enough to know that a cloth sunflower may not be the best DPC challenge subject. ;)  Next time, splurge for the real thing at the florist.</td>', 'Technicals:  I think there is a color cast here.  The middle of the flower looks "off" to me.  It is either that or actual oversaturation.  Sometimes we jack that saturation up just too far (and I''m as guilty of that as anybody).  Composition may have improved without the second sunflower in the corner. The feel:  I mentioned this on another Fill the Frame, but what is the purpose of the tight crop other than to meet the challenge?  The best pictures in this challenge conveyed something by their tight crop. The game:  OK, you''ve been around long enough to know that a cloth sunflower may not be the best DPC challenge subject. ;)  Next time, splurge for the real thing at the florist.', '2007-09-10 21:39:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4080010, 577537, 46993, '<td valign="top">Great shot, soft but clean- the lighting really does add to the overall tone which is warm and perfect match for subject. Nice, nice photo.</td>', 'Great shot, soft but clean- the lighting really does add to the overall tone which is warm and perfect match for subject. Nice, nice photo.', '2007-09-11 01:45:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(4080383, 577586, 68797, '<td valign="top">I saw you post this in Dr.Achoo''s thread. <br/> <br/>I gave you a 4 for this one. Why?<br/> <br/>first of all because of the crop. it''s too narrow on the short side. this makes me think there was a lot of uninteresting stuff going on around it and you just cut out the best part. but with doing that you cut of his ears, paws, basically the whole body. If you want to get an extreme close up to fill the frame, make sure it''s sharp enough to crop it all the way to the face. now it looks like you had to do some pretty extensive PP for it too look acceptable.<br/> <br/>the partial desat...i really don''t like it.<br/> <br/>having taken everything in consideration, this photo looks like a shot that you have tried to polish up in PP but it just didn''t work.<br/> <br/>personally I would''ve chucked it away.<br/> <br/>so, there you have my honest opinion as to why I gave this a 4.</td>', 'I saw you post this in Dr.Achoo''s thread.  I gave you a 4 for this one. Why? first of all because of the crop. it''s too narrow on the short side. this makes me think there was a lot of uninteresting stuff going on around it and you just cut out the best part. but with doing that you cut of his ears, paws, basically the whole body. If you want to get an extreme close up to fill the frame, make sure it''s sharp enough to crop it all the way to the face. now it looks like you had to do some pretty extensive PP for it too look acceptable. the partial desat...i really don''t like it. having taken everything in consideration, this photo looks like a shot that you have tried to polish up in PP but it just didn''t work. personally I would''ve chucked it away. so, there you have my honest opinion as to why I gave this a 4.', '2007-09-11 08:07:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4080674, 577537, 74605, '<td valign="top">Beautiful portrait!  The light, colors, composition, and textures are all great!  Well done.</td>', 'Beautiful portrait!  The light, colors, composition, and textures are all great!  Well done.', '2007-09-11 10:17:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4081423, 577725, 43410, '<td valign="top">how is this different from using a really heavy vignetting?<br/> <br/>i''m very confused at the moment as well...still...your talent as a photographer is not in question, VERY nice image. <br/> <br/>fav</td>', 'how is this different from using a really heavy vignetting? i''m very confused at the moment as well...still...your talent as a photographer is not in question, VERY nice image.  fav', '2007-09-11 15:41:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4081731, 577586, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals:  There is something about the sharpness, and I think it''s the tungsten lighting.  The problem with using such a warm light (and I know it wasn''t your choice) is you are using less of the sensor since red makes up only 1/3rd of the pixels.  Anyways, there is a sharpness quality to this picture that lets it down somewhat.  Composition is just fine, even with the extreme landscape crop.<br/> <br/>The feel: You lose some intimacy with the tiger''s right eye being in shadow.  Fill flash or waiting for a different moment are your only options there.<br/> <br/>The game: Tigers seem to be a good subject on DPC.  I''d head back to get this guy again later if you can.</td>', 'Technicals:  There is something about the sharpness, and I think it''s the tungsten lighting.  The problem with using such a warm light (and I know it wasn''t your choice) is you are using less of the sensor since red makes up only 1/3rd of the pixels.  Anyways, there is a sharpness quality to this picture that lets it down somewhat.  Composition is just fine, even with the extreme landscape crop. The feel: You lose some intimacy with the tiger''s right eye being in shadow.  Fill flash or waiting for a different moment are your only options there. The game: Tigers seem to be a good subject on DPC.  I''d head back to get this guy again later if you can.', '2007-09-11 17:52:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4083471, 577597, 20608, '<td valign="top">I think one of your best macros to date.. the spelling in the title got you a few down votes I bet... although it shouldn''t</td>', 'I think one of your best macros to date.. the spelling in the title got you a few down votes I bet... although it shouldn''t', '2007-09-12 04:42:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4084412, 577660, 53572, '<td valign="top">it''s the words, innit?<br/> <br/>this is just so...kerouac, baker, beat bar scene, yeah.<br/> <br/>this should be very big indeed.</td>', 'it''s the words, innit? this is just so...kerouac, baker, beat bar scene, yeah. this should be very big indeed.', '2007-09-12 12:20:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4084736, 576316, 65319, '<td valign="top">WooooW!  That eye is just astounding.  Composition is such a hallmark of your photography especially when enhanced by your excellent eye for color makes this photo truly beautiful.  Well done!</td>', 'WooooW!  That eye is just astounding.  Composition is such a hallmark of your photography especially when enhanced by your excellent eye for color makes this photo truly beautiful.  Well done!', '2007-09-12 14:12:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(4084769, 577597, 3569, '<td valign="top">This should have done much better.  I like the daddy with the parasitic mite.  Quite nice.  Van</td>', 'This should have done much better.  I like the daddy with the parasitic mite.  Quite nice.  Van', '2007-09-12 14:26:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(4086153, 577697, 75034, '<td valign="top">Sorry to see the DQ but glad to see you didn''t leave the site. I liked this in the challenge and totally got what you were trying to do with the title. It clicked with me right away. The shot was very nicely done and the contrast of the sepia tones on your face then the B&amp;W and back to your eyes in green and brown was a great touch. <br/> <br/>Hope to see something from you again in an upcoming challenge.<br/> <br/>MAX!</td>', 'Sorry to see the DQ but glad to see you didn''t leave the site. I liked this in the challenge and totally got what you were trying to do with the title. It clicked with me right away. The shot was very nicely done and the contrast of the sepia tones on your face then the B&W and back to your eyes in green and brown was a great touch.  Hope to see something from you again in an upcoming challenge. MAX!', '2007-09-12 23:22:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(4086444, 576316, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, that neck and that EYE!</td>', 'Wow, that neck and that EYE!', '2007-09-13 00:57:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(4086656, 577725, 62815, '<td valign="top">GREAT ,GREAT ,GREAT,It must had been a ribbon winner.But who has gave you 1,2,3 even 4 to this one? From time to time i thinking if anyone of them has ever take a photo like this one .I don''t think so.....I saw your ribbons and i can not copy one of them for the challenge, i will try with someone else  :)</td>', 'GREAT ,GREAT ,GREAT,It must had been a ribbon winner.But who has gave you 1,2,3 even 4 to this one? From time to time i thinking if anyone of them has ever take a photo like this one .I don''t think so.....I saw your ribbons and i can not copy one of them for the challenge, i will try with someone else  :)', '2007-09-13 04:03:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4087692, 577187, 60862, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your OOBie!</td>', 'Congrats on your OOBie!', '2007-09-13 15:52:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4088179, 577675, 41047, '<td valign="top">amazing dof, this is lovely and should have scored much higher.</td>', 'amazing dof, this is lovely and should have scored much higher.', '2007-09-13 20:51:36.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(4090085, 575582, 14476, '<td valign="top">es, this is one of those times when you can only gasp a bit, then shrug your shoulders and let go.  <br/> <br/>Of course you have a gorgeous portrait here and except for a ''cat bias'' it could easily have been on the front page.   It has technique, originality and that ''wow'' factor that is much appreciated ordinarily.</td>', 'es, this is one of those times when you can only gasp a bit, then shrug your shoulders and let go.   Of course you have a gorgeous portrait here and except for a ''cat bias'' it could easily have been on the front page.   It has technique, originality and that ''wow'' factor that is much appreciated ordinarily.', '2007-09-14 14:38:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(4094230, 577519, 48928, '<td valign="top">I like this, nice sharp focus and the color tones work very well...</td>', 'I like this, nice sharp focus and the color tones work very well...', '2007-09-16 17:34:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4095075, 576487, 34938, '<td valign="top">I knew what it was...nice shot...</td>', 'I knew what it was...nice shot...', '2007-09-17 00:48:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4095348, 577442, 68504, '<td valign="top">Compelling photo/portrait.  (Maybe not worried but thoughtful or even just plain refreshingly real).  Your desat is just right.</td>', 'Compelling photo/portrait.  (Maybe not worried but thoughtful or even just plain refreshingly real).  Your desat is just right.', '2007-09-17 02:01:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4096407, 577519, 62318, '<td valign="top">You are very good with the technicals. I love the mono-chromatic color used here. The detail is superb and this would make a terrific product placement shot.</td>', 'You are very good with the technicals. I love the mono-chromatic color used here. The detail is superb and this would make a terrific product placement shot.', '2007-09-17 12:50:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4096481, 576316, 62318, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, if I didn''t know better I would swear this bird was stuffed. :) Gorgeous color and framing.</td>', 'Beautiful shot, if I didn''t know better I would swear this bird was stuffed. :) Gorgeous color and framing.', '2007-09-17 13:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4098210, 577156, 75713, '<td valign="top">What a beautiful shot... voted lower than what I would have thought... it looks like a painting.. the colors are magnificant.</td>', 'What a beautiful shot... voted lower than what I would have thought... it looks like a painting.. the colors are magnificant.', '2007-09-18 02:15:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(4099138, 576092, 29490, '<td valign="top">Hot chicks rule!!! Hubba :)<br/> <br/>errrr - I mean ... nice photo, ma''am :)</td>', 'Hot chicks rule!!! Hubba :) errrr - I mean ... nice photo, ma''am :)', '2007-09-18 15:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4099366, 576997, 29011, '<td valign="top">The lilly flower looks a little too bright in some spots but it''s a very nice eye pleasing shot. Impressionism came to mind when first viewing it, especially with the recent challenge. Would''ve been perfect for that challenge.</td>', 'The lilly flower looks a little too bright in some spots but it''s a very nice eye pleasing shot. Impressionism came to mind when first viewing it, especially with the recent challenge. Would''ve been perfect for that challenge.', '2007-09-18 17:21:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4102831, 577685, 41047, '<td valign="top">:) this is very cool.</td>', ':) this is very cool.', '2007-09-19 19:12:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4107448, 576888, 16241, '<td valign="top">Katherine Kelly Lang from the bold and the beautiful.<br/>:)</td>', 'Katherine Kelly Lang from the bold and the beautiful.:)', '2007-09-21 17:30:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(4111886, 577052, 30982, '<td valign="top">I LOVE this!  And I''m horribly envious about the whole light deal - really does give exceptional catchlights, doesn''t it?  And the high key is very well done.  She certainly has the most extraordinary eyes.</td>', 'I LOVE this!  And I''m horribly envious about the whole light deal - really does give exceptional catchlights, doesn''t it?  And the high key is very well done.  She certainly has the most extraordinary eyes.', '2007-09-24 07:14:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(4125652, 577567, 14986, '<td valign="top">The pink just jumped out at me, looking at the thumbnails.  This is really pretty.  Although it doesn''t fill the frame as much as it could, outside of the challenge it''s a shot that stands well on its own.</td>', 'The pink just jumped out at me, looking at the thumbnails.  This is really pretty.  Although it doesn''t fill the frame as much as it could, outside of the challenge it''s a shot that stands well on its own.', '2007-09-30 09:30:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4136094, 577717, 62318, '<td valign="top">Wow, amazing colors. I like the brown with the sea-green blue. The textures are amazing.</td>', 'Wow, amazing colors. I like the brown with the sea-green blue. The textures are amazing.', '2007-10-03 03:20:24.000000', NULL, 0),
